Below is a comprehensive guide to creating a fully-featured Magento theme that updates your website's design, navigation, and product page layout while maintaining responsiveness and optimization.

## Step 1: Theme Directory Structure

Create your theme directory under `app/design/frontend`:

```
app/
└── design/
    └── frontend/
        └── YourVendor/
            └── YourTheme/
                ├── etc/
                │   └── theme.xml
                ├── registration.php
                ├── web/
                │   ├── css/
                │   ├── fonts/
                │   └── images/
                ├── Magento_Theme/
                │   └── layout/
                ├── Magento_Catalog/
                │   └── layout/
                └── templates/
```

## Step 2: Registration File

Create `registration.php` in your theme root:

```php
<?php
\Magento\Framework\Component\ComponentRegistrar::register(
    \Magento\Framework\Component\ComponentRegistrar::THEME,
    'frontend/YourVendor/YourTheme',
    __DIR__
);
```

## Step 3: Theme Configuration

Create `etc/theme.xml`:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<theme xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" 
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:Config/etc/theme.xsd">
    <title>Your Theme Name</title>
    <parent>Magento/blank</parent> <!-- or luma, for blank base -->
    <media>
        <preview_image>media/preview.jpg</preview_image>
    </media>
</theme>
```

## Step 4: Custom Layout Updates

### Product Page Customization

Create `Magento_Catalog/layout/catalog_product_view.xml`:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <!-- Move elements or customize page structure -->
        <move element="product.info.main" destination="product.info.container" before="-"/>
        <move element="product.info.details" destination="product.info.main" after="product.info.price"/>

        <!-- Remove default reviews section -->
        <referenceBlock name="product.info.review" remove="true"/>
    </body>
</page>
```

### Header Customization

Create `Magento_Theme/layout/default.xml`:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      layout="1column"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <!-- Customize logo and navigation -->
        <referenceContainer name="header-wrapper">
            <container name="custom.header" as="customHeader" label="Custom Header"/>
        </referenceContainer>

        <referenceContainer name="custom.header">
            <block class="Magento\Theme\Block\Html\Header\Logo" name="logo" after="-"/>
            <block class="Magento\Theme\Block\Html\Topmenu" name="catalog.topnav" template="Magento_Theme::html/topmenu.phtml"/>
        </referenceContainer>
    </body>
</page>
```

## Step 5: CSS and Styling

Create your main CSS file at `web/css/source/_extend.less`:

```less
@charset 'UTF-8';

//
// Theme Color Scheme
//

@primary-color: #004080; // Update to your brand color
@secondary-color: #007aff;
@link-color: @primary-color;
@success-color: #45a048;

// Typography
@font-family-name: 'Inter', sans-serif;
@font-family-base: @font-family-name, @font-family-fallback;

body {
    font-family: @font-family-name;
    color: #333;
    background-color: @body-bg;
}

button, .action.primary {
    background-color: @primary-color;
    border-radius: 4px;
    &:hover {
        background-color: darken(@primary-color, 10%);
    }
}

// Product Page Styling
.product-info-price .price {
    color: @primary-color;
    font-size: 24px;
}

.product.info.detailed {
    margin-top: 40px;
    h2 {
        font-size: 28px;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
}
```

## Step 6: Typography and Font Integration

Update `web/css/source/_extend.less` with font imports:

```less
@font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    src: url('@{baseDir}fonts/Inter-VariableFont.woff2') format('woff2');
    font-weight: 100 900;
    font-display: swap;
}
```

## Step 7: Responsive Design

Add responsive breakpoints to your `_extend.less`:

```less
@mobile-breakpoint: 768px;

@media only screen and (max-width: @mobile-breakpoint) {
    .responsive-nav-toggle {
        display: block;
    }

    .nav {
        display: none;
    }
